---
description: Hard risk invariants that apply to all code
alwaysApply: true
---
- Max risk per trade: 0.5% of equity (vol-targeted). Max gross exposure: 2.0x. Max net: 1.0x.
- Daily loss limit: -2.5% → flatten all, halt until next UTC day.
- Trailing drawdown limit: -8% from HWM → halt, require human re-enable.
- Position sizing: fractional Kelly at f = 0.25 × Kelly, capped by vol target of 15% annualised.
- No new risk 15 min before / 30 min after scheduled Tier-1 macro events (FOMC, CPI, NFP).
- Any code touching risk/ or execution/ needs a test that proves the limit triggers.
- If you are unsure whether a change weakens a limit, stop and ask the human.
- The canonical values live in `risk/limits.py::RiskLimits`. Changing a default there is a
  constitution change: it requires the human's explicit approval in the PR description.
